course: dictionary
lesson: 12094
title: Minibeasts: the cockchafer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cockchafer is a large brown beetle from Europe. People also call it a May bug or a doodlebug. «On a warm May evening, a cockchafer bumped into the kitchen window.» The clue is in the words around it: warm, May, evening, and bumped. Those words tell you it is a flying insect that is out in spring.
explain: Cockchafers fly clumsily, so they seem to tumble through the air. They also buzz loudly. «The cockchafer buzzed past the lamp.» If you hear a loud buzz on a spring evening, you might be hearing one.
explain: The young cockchafer is not a beetle at all. It is a fat white grub that lives in the soil. «The cockchafer grubs ate the roots of the lawn.» Here the grubs are the young stage, and the beetle is the adult.
fact: A cockchafer is a large brown beetle found in Europe.
fact: Cockchafers are also called May bugs or doodlebugs.
fact: A cockchafer grub is fat and white, and it lives in the soil.
fact: Cockchafer grubs eat plant roots.
fact: In the life cycle of a cockchafer, the grubs can live underground for three or four years before they become adults.
exercise: «On a warm May evening, a cockchafer bumped into the kitchen window.» What is a cockchafer? | *A large brown beetle that flies on spring evenings | A fish that swims in ponds | A small green bird | A kind of tall tree
exercise: «The cockchafer grubs ate the roots of the lawn.» What do the grubs eat? | Bread crumbs | Other flies | *Plant roots | Leaves from the trees
exercise: Which is another name for the cockchafer? | *Doodlebug | Honey bee | Ladybird | Stag beetle
test: What does a cockchafer grub look like? | *A fat white grub | A black spider | A thin green worm | A red flying insect
test: In the life cycle of a cockchafer, what comes after the larva (grub)? | Caterpillar | *Pupa | Tadpole | Egg
exam: How long can cockchafer grubs live underground? | Less than one day | Exactly one week | Only during the summer | *Three or four years
